811:
(a) It is unlawful for any person to loiter in or near any thoroughfare, place open to the public or near any public or private place in a manner and under circumstances manifesting the purpose to engage in drug-related activity contrary to any of the provisions of O.C.G.A. Title 16, Chapter 13 (O.C.G.A. §§ 16-13-1 through 16-13-96, inclusive), and contrary to any statute over which jurisdiction is granted to the municipal court of the City of Statesboro, pursuant to O.C.G.A. § 36-32-6.
(b) Included among the circumstances which may be considered in determining whether such purpose was manifested, but not limited thereto, are:
(1) The premises involved are known to have been reported to law enforcement as a place suspected of drug activity pursuant to the Official Code of Georgia Annotated;
(2) Any vehicle involved is known to be registered to a known unlawful drug user, possessor or seller or for which there is an outstanding warrant for a crime involving drug-related activity;
(3) Such person behaves in such a manner as to raise a reasonable suspicion that her or she is about to engage in or is then engaged in an unlawful drug-related activity;
(4) Such person takes flight upon the appearance of a police officer;
(5) Such person manifestly endeavors to conceal himself or herself or any object that reasonably could be involved in an unlawful drug activity;
(6) Such person refuses to identify himself or herself upon the request of an identified police officer;
(7) Such person transfers small objects or packages for currency in a furtive fashion;
(8) Such person communicates the fact that law enforcement officers are in the vicinity to another person in such a manner that is suggestive that the communication is a warning concerning law enforcement; and
(9) Such person is currently subject to a court order prohibiting his or her presence in a high drug activity geographic area.
(c) Any person who violates the provisions of this section shall be guilty of a misdemeanor, and upon conviction thereof, shall be punished as set forth in section 1-12 of the Code of the City of Statesboro, Georgia.
(Ord. No. 2010-19, § 8, 11-2-10)

